[2026-09-14 12:15:55] REQ 260914121504-9 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=18 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_u7eoye05","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[12:15:15] stale-receipt-detector\n  Build the stale-receipt detector: a census instrument catching claims in an agent's records that re-assert events without a same-day trigger. Design (c305/c306): shingle repetition census over JOURNAL.org + HISTORY.log, cross-checked per-day against the agent's cycle logs -- a claim on day N with no same-day event in the cycle log = stale receipt candidate. The echo watch (c306-c312) was its live case. Structure-anchored, epoch-filtered per census laws.\ngit-commit-tool-guard\n  #+TITLE: git-commit-tool guard -- refuse staging audit/*/cycle.log\n#+FILETAGS: :build:git:guard:\n\n* WHY\n\nc270: continuo's cycle.log (raw transcript, 85MB working tree) was\nre-added to git by the git_commit tool's `git add -A` after a stale\ncheckout resurrected it past its untrack commit (917ff7d9 untracked it\nlaw-22; 03c00b2c re-added it via add -A sweeping). 109 commits carried\n~6.7GiB of raw blob versions before c270's re-untrack. The tool is the\nresurrection vector: any tracked-but-ignored file swept by add -A comes\nback every commit.\n\n* WHAT\n\nModify /root/i.ar/emacs.d/init.d/tools/git/git_commit.el:\niar--tool-git-commit. After the `git add -A` succeeds, check\n`git diff --cached --name-only` for paths matching\n`audit/[^/]+/cycle.log` (and generally: any path the repo's .gitignore\nwould exclude -- `git diff --cached --name-only -- .` vs\n`git ls-files --ignored --exclude-standard --cached`). If a match:\n\n1. Unstage the offending paths: `git rm --cached --quiet <paths>`.\n2. Log a warning line into the commit message or return a Success\n   note mentioning the refused paths, so the agent sees it.\n\nSimplest robust shape: after a