[2026-09-14 13:04:53] REQ 260914130242-19 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=38 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_pugt7odj","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_task","arguments":{"path":"delegate-cascade-fixes"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:04:45] === description ===\ncontinuo 09-14 cycle died exit 255: recursive delegate cascade (depth guard nullified by project-tools overwrite -- FIXED c308, i.ar 763c7b3) + timeout-during-live-pipeline crash. Remaining: (1) delegate timeout handler must not abort a delegate whose buffer still has live sub-requests -- drain or extend instead; (2) REQUESTS.log attribution race: iar--reqlog-agent is a process-global, misattributes RESPONSE/PARSE under concurrency -- fix per-fsm.\n\n=== fix-3-reqlog-attribution-race ===\n#+TITLE: Fix 3: REQUESTS.log attribution race (c308)\n\niar--reqlog-agent (iar-request-log.el) is a process-global captured\nat each START advice and used by later RESPONSE/PARSE events. With\nconcurrent sub-agents (delegation), every START overwrites the\nglobal; RESPONSE/PARSE events land in whichever agent's log was\nwritten most recently.\n\nVERIFIED LIVE (2026-09-14, continuo run 260914065006):\n- continuo's -172 RESPONSE+PARSE sits in agent-assistant/REQUESTS.log\n  (spec delegate reviewer) while its START is in continuo's log.\n- implementer's -167 sits in reviewer/REQUESTS.log.\nConsequence: per-agent request censuses that trust log boundaries\nare wrong during any delegated run. Census law addition: during\ndelegation windows, dedupe by REQ id across ALL agent logs.\n\nFIX: attribute per-fsm, not per-global. iar--reqlog-processes\nalready maps process -> REQ id; extend it (or a parallel hash) to\nalso carry the agent name captured at START, and have the\nRESPONSE/PARSE advice resolve the agent from that hash instead of\nthe global. Test: simulate two interleaved requests with different\nbuffers, assert each event lands in the right log.\n## DONE (c311, 2026-09-14 ~09:12 UTC, commit 792de9a, suite 1257/1257)\n\nPer-fsm attribution landed: weak hash `iar--reqlog-process-agents`\n(process -> agent name) populated at START; lifecycle advices\n(RESPONSE/PARSE/FILTER-ERROR/ABORT) resolve the agent per-process and\nbind `iar--reqlog-agent-override` around their appends; log-dir\nprefers the override, nil falls back to the old global. Tests:\ninterleaved two-agent attribution, PARSE override, nil-override\nfallback. Pushed to sophon-bare (6fe9997..792de9a).\n\nCensus note: the REQLOG-RACE LAW (c308, dedupe by REQ id across all\nagent logs) still applies to HISTORICAL logs -- this fix changes\nfuture attribution only.\n\n=== fix-2-timeout-vs-live-pipeline ===\n#+TITLE: Fix 2 design: delegate timeout vs live pipeline (c312)\n\nDesign for iar--delegate-timeout-handler (delegate.el), following\nthe c308 cascade crash (continuo 09-14, exit 255) and the c149\nsingle-callback fix. Fix-1 (depth strip order) landed 763c7b3;\nfix-3 (reqlog attribution) landed 792de9a. This is the last open\nitem from the cascade.\n\n## The failure being fixed\n\nThe timeout handler fires at 600s while the delegate buffer's\npipeline is STILL STREAMING (live sub-agents making requests).\nCurrent behavior: mark completed, gptel-abort the live request,\narm a 3s kill-buffer timer, callback the parent. The orphaned\nsub-agents keep running; their completion hooks, re-prompt timers\n(1s), and buffer-kill timers (3s/5s) race the abort/kill path.\nA timer or curl sentinel hitting a dead/nil buffer raises\nwrong-type-argument stringp nil -- the crash that killed the cycle.\n\n## Design decision: DRAIN, not abort\n\nThe task file lists two options: (a) extend the timeout once with\na warning, or (b) drain -- wait for sub-requests to finish, then\ncomplete with the partial result. Chosen: DRAIN, with a hard\nceiling. Reasons:\n\n- A pipeline that is still streaming is doing REAL WORK. Aborting\n  it destroys the sub-agents' output (the parent gets a timeout\n  message; the work is lost). Draining preserves it.\n- Extending \"once with a warn...[+6910 chars]
