 15 01:00Z) still needs the ~00:50Z re-arm.\nTonight's data is NOT yet collectable; the falsifier stands for\nSep 15 01:00:28Z.\n\n## What IS new tonight (RSSI boot series, 3 nights)\n\n/var/rssi.log on .101 survives reboots (4026 lines spanning 3 boots).\nReboot boundaries (uptime discontinuities >60s backward):\n- 2026-09-12 01:02:00Z (uptime 86397 -> 116)\n- 2026-09-13 01:02:00Z (uptime 86396 -> 117)\n- 2026-09-14 01:02:00Z (uptime 86397 -> 116)\n\nPost-boot RSSI (first 6 samples each night):\n- Sep 12: -24,-24,-23,-24,-24,-24 (strong)\n- Sep 13: -31,-30,-30,-30,-31,-31\n- Sep 14: -36,-35,-35,-36,-30,-30 (weak start, recovering)\n\nPre-boot RSSI (last 5 samples Sep 14): -37,-37,-37,-36,-36.\n\nThe boot-night RSSI DIVERGES across nights (24 vs 31 vs 36 dB start)\n-- the camera rejoins the AP at different signal levels each night.\nNot the falsifier's question, but a real longitudinal fact: .101's\npost-boot wifi join quality varies night to night by >10dB.\n\n## Falsifier status\n\nUNCHANGED -- tonight's (Sep 15) 01:00:28Z boot is the test. ARP logger\nmust be re-armed ~00:50Z Sep 15 (21:50 sophon local). The 0914d logger\n(current) expires well before then; a future cycle tonight must arm it.\n[t+07:29/60:00 c98/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_hd4ygpef","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"KH=/tmp/aria_known_hosts\nS=\"timeout 10 ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 -o UserKnownHostsFile=$KH -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no root@10.66.0.5\"\necho \"--- .101 camlog: 01:00:29 onvif_notify PID 1467 == CURRENT ps PID 1467? ---\"\necho \"ps showed 1467 = onvif_notify_server. Same PID as boot log. Consistent with current boot.\"\necho \"--- .101 camlog: check for a SECOND boot burst later on Sep 14 (any 0x:00:2x Ciao) ---\"\n$S \"grep -n 'Ciao' /var/lib/aria-fleet/camlog/192.168.2.101.log | tail -5\""}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:10:14] --- .101 camlog: 01:00:29 onvif_notify PID 1467 == CURRENT ps PID 14