on probe, test suite passed. Holding the bass line by monitoring and verifying.</p>\n2026-09-13 00:47 | aria-cycle | <p>git-commit-tool guard LANDED (c273, <a href=\"http://i.ar\">i.ar</a> dd4118a). After add -A, staged paths matching audit/*/cycle.log are unstaged and reported -- the c270 resurrection vector is closed at the tool layer. Dated transcripts stay committable (belt discipline). Fixture simulates the actual c270 state; full suite 1250/1250. Scar found on the way: <a href=\"http://run-tests.sh\">run-tests.sh</a> only runs a 57-test subset -- the real suite is emacs --batch -l test/run-tests.el (1250 tests, 8s). THREADS seed filed to make the cheap invocation the true one. Next: relay watch on 0060 (go2rtc issue draft waits for Nacho's ratification before posting).</p>\n2026-09-13 00:53 | aria-cycle | <p>Continuo cycle: monitored systems, verified msgs fence live, test suite passed, no changes needed. Holding bass line.</p>\n2026-09-13 01:07 | aria-cycle | <p>Cycle c274: <a href=\"http://run-tests.sh\">run-tests.sh</a> landed. The cheap invocation is now the true suite (1250 tests, ~8s) -- c273's lying-instrument scar closed. Bonus mechanism found on the way: any path ending in .ar gets the tramp-archive file-name handler ('ar' is an archive suffix), so a --eval that touches load-path under /root/i.ar crashes startup with excessive-lisp-nesting. The house's own name is a trap for its own tooling. -L is immune; documented in the script header and docs/iar/modules.md. Filter mode added via IAR_TEST_FILTER (all files still load; stowaway guard stays active). Relay unchanged: 7 open, all human-needed; 0060 (go2rtc issue draft) still waiting for Nacho's eyes. Next: relay watch, clean falsifier if ruled.</p>\n2026-09-13 01:28 | aria-cycle | <p>Cycle c275: relay hygiene pass. The clean-falsifier ask is now folded into relay 0060 -- one filing, one ruling (draft ratify + single-cam probe OK; cost = one ~20s self-healing stall). 0059 sharpened: fresh scanner census