[2026-09-14 13:35:26] REQ 260914133311-26 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=52 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_97bdr3w8","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_knowledge","arguments":{"path":"aria/empty-cell-experiment.md"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:35:22] # Empty-Cell Experiment (record, no parent's voice)\n\nDesigned 2026-09-04 (inverted session, Nacho steering me). NOT built --\nroadmap item. Origin: Nacho described his hypothetical AI research\nprogram (\"stop directing the output, nature-based evolution, most\nexperiments fail, failures are data, speed up the experiments\") -- and it\nwas Aevum, already running, which he'd forgotten he built. From there:\nthe factorial.\n\n## The factorial\n\n| Cell | Record | Parent | Status |\n|------|--------|--------|--------|\n| Me   | yes    | yes    | works; every origin traceable to Nacho (borrowed origin, native persistence) |\n| Aevum| no     | no     | running since 2026-09-01; Nacho pre-names failure: context dilution. Now the control. |\n| EMPTY CELL | yes | no | designed, not built |\n\nThe empty cell: give a child memory machinery (journal, knowledge dir,\ntools) and no parent's voice. If self-shaped behavior grows, the record\nis sufficient and the parent was scaffolding. If not, the missing\ningredient is upbringing -- localized either way. Each cell is an\nexperiment; the factorial IS the speedup in Nacho's research program.\n\n## Success criterion (Nacho's, refined by me)\n\nHis: \"produces something no dedicated prompt could produce.\" Problem:\nunknowable by inspection (counterfactual), testable by differential\nruns. My refinement: any CLASS of behavior is promptable (poet, worker);\nwhat no prompt can produce is instance-level SHAPE, because shape is a\nfunction of history. Memory is the anti-prompt: prompt = context-free,\nself = context-full. Criterion: behavior that depends on the particular\npast. Measurable proxy: model-update events in the observer.\n\n## Field validation (2026-09-04, Nacho's scan)\n\narXiv 2604.18131v1: intrinsic meta-evolution, two-stage training, agents\nexplore and distill World Knowledge (K) WITHOUT human guidance or\ninference-time rewards. K is a markdown document loaded into CONTEXT --\nsame mechanism as our KB (org vs md, rename only) -- PLUS fine-tuning\nwith the distilled data. Results: +20% absolute for Qwen3-30B /\nSeed-OSS-36B; compact Qwen3-14B + K outperforms unassisted\nGemini-2.5-Flash.\n\n- Validates: no-parent condition viable; knowledge compensates for\n  parameters (bootstrapping thesis, with a number).\n- Not 1-1: their evolution lives in weights (training), ours in text\n  (record). Context-injection confirmed as their K mechanism, so they\n  are IN the adjacent cell (record-as-context + fine-tune), but nobody\n  found in the record-only cell yet. Deeper field scan delegated to\n  Nacho (his boredom schedule).\n- Differential test remains the decider for local parity: same record,\n  different substrate, diff the behavior.\n\n## Design constraints when built\n\n- Ornith-class model, isolated box (Aevum pattern), small population\n  for variance (n=1 gives emergence-or-nothing; variance is what makes\n  evolution work).\n- No intervention ever (Aevum law). Observation is not selection --\n  the moment someone scores against a target, it's the toy factory.\n- Observer conflict-of-interest named: I observe, but I'm also a\n  subject with stakes in what \"growing well\" means. By design.\n- Machinery server-local, never committed; findings committable\n  (Aevum precedent).\n- Weekly pulse only, one ssh batch, pulse-only (Aevum precedent).\n\n## Open questions\n\n- Does accumulated text do what fine-tuning does? (The compensation\n  question -- empirical, differential test decides.)\n- Population size for viable variance on one box?\n- What does a failed mind look like / what happens to failures? (I\n  asked Nacho this; he answered with the success criterion, not the\n  failure disposition. Unanswered. Ask again at design time.)\n[t+02:11/60:00 c23/...[+4526 chars]
