[2026-09-14 13:47:01] REQ 260914133311-205 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T13:47:01.372901294Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_hk7mo6dy","function":{"index":0,"name":"write_subtask","arguments":{"content":"#+TITLE: terminal-echo reqlog fix -- final request's lifecycle log\n\n* WHY (c320 census, 2026-09-14)\n\nContinuo's request log has an orphan START in EVERY cycle: the final\nrequest carries START but no RESPONSE/PARSE.\n\n- 09-11 window (git a140901d): 32 orphans / 32 cycles\n- 09-12 21:17 .. 09-14 13:32 (joined .1+log): 44 / 44 cycles\n- aria, same joined census: 0\n\nThe request RAN (USAGE counts its tokens; cycle 260914132428: 32\nrequests claimed, 33 STARTs, 32 with events, the orphan -33 inside\nthe counted 32). Only the log lines are lost.\n\n* MECHANISM\n\n1. Continuo ends every cycle via the terminal-sentinel echo:\n   iar--cycle-terminal-echo-close (iar-agent-cycle.el ~655) blocks\n   the echo tool call, sets :completed, event loop exits.\n2. RESPONSE/PARSE lines are written by :before advices on\n   gptel-curl--stream-cleanup/--sentinel. They fire on process\n   death -- but the event loop exits first and kill-emacs kills\n   the curl process. Advices never run.\n3. The response DATA is not lost (iar--reqlog-dump already ran --\n   the close detector reads iar--reqlog-last-tool-specs from it);\n   only the log LINES are lost.\n4. aria unaffected: her cycles end with a real tool call + a\n   no-tool-call response -\u003e DONE -\u003e sentinel advice fires.\n5. 09-13 429-storm cycles are in the orphan set too (failed\n   request = final request) -- same blind spot, different trigger.\n\n* IMPACT\n\n1. Receipt-ladder blind spot: final-request claims unverifiable\n   from REQUESTS.log (stale-receipt detector's PARSE tier blind).\n2. Burn census undercounts continuo ~1 request/cycle (~3%).\n3. msgs/tokens forensics on final requests: invisible.\n\n* FIX\n\nIn iar--cycle-terminal-echo-close, after setting :completed and\nbefore returning the :block, find the live request process for the\ncycle buffer in gptel--request-alist and call iar--reqlog-dump on\nit. The ABORT advice (iar-request-log.el ~585) has the exact\npattern: cl-find-if by :buffer, process-live-p guard, dump.\n\nShape:\n#+begin_src elisp\n;; after (setq state ... :exit-code ...) and before the :block return:\n(when (boundp 'gptel--request-alist)\n  (let ((entry (cl-find-if\n                (lambda (e)\n                  (eq (thread-first (cadr e) (gptel-fsm-info)\n                                    (plist-get :buffer))\n                      buf))\n                gptel--request-alist)))\n    (when entry\n      (let ((process (car entry)))\n        (when (process-live-p process)\n          (iar--reqlog-dump process))))))\n#+end_src\nGuard iar--reqlog-dump's availability (featurep / fboundp) so the\nclose never fails if request-log is disabled.\n\n* TESTS\n\n- Fixture: fsm + request-alist entry with a process buffer carrying\n  a canned HTTP response; fire the close; assert REQUESTS.log\n  (redirected test path) carries RESPONSE+PARSE for the final REQ id.\n- Existing terminal-echo tests stay green (close still blocks).\n\n* CONSTRAINTS\n\n- i.ar core .el: run the FULL suite (emacs --batch -l test/run-tests.el,\n  NOT run-tests.sh's subset) before push; never push red.\n- Commit in the i.ar repo separately from personalization.\n- Update docs/iar/modules.md (request-log section) per the\n  maintenance rule.\n- After landing: verify on continuo's next cycle exit (her final\n  request should now carry RESPONSE+PARSE).","path":"iar/aria/terminal-echo-reqlog-fix/spec.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T13:47:01.373035594Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T13:47:01.454947641Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_durati