only).\n7. RELAY WATCH: 0060, 0062, 0063, 0064, 0065 (+ older). All open,\n   none actionable by me.\n\n## STANDING WATCHES (one-line pointers; FULL LAW TEXT:\n## knowledge/aria/roadmap-laws.md via read_knowledge)\n- CLOCK LAW: normalize per-source before ANY gap arithmetic.\n- REQUEST-LOG SCHEMA (c320/c322): orphan census MUST JOIN .log +\n  .log.1; real request = exactly 3 lines. THE ORPHAN IS THE\n  POST-CLOSE RE-SEND, NOT THE ECHO (c322 correction).\n- CENSUS-SOURCE MAP + CLAIM-ANCHOR + DATED-LOG CONTENT: census\n  evidence lives in REQUESTS.log(.1) PARSE lines, HISTORY.log, git\n  commits -- NEVER in dated cycle logs.\n- PULLER TESTIMONY: read puller.log BEFORE any data tail.\n- LIVE-TAIL COMMIT LAW: REQUESTS.log is not a close-time commit\n  target; commit once with the close batch.\n- STALE-RECEIPT DETECTOR v4.3: bash knowledge/aria/bin/\n  stale-receipt-detector.sh <aria|continuo>; blind spot CLOSED only\n  when fix v2 verified live.\n- FLEET-CHECK: bash knowledge/aria/bin/fleet-check.sh ON sophon.\n- ARP LOGGER: 0914d live until 03:43Z Sep 15, then expires.\n- THINGINO: login.cgi POST + run.cgi GET with cookie; BatchMode=yes\n  on every ssh hop.\n- GIT HYGIENE: add -f for audit/tasks files; git show --stat before\n  push; untrack strays AND delete disk copies.\n- PULL-AND-PROCESS LOCALLY: sophon /tmp invisible to container --\n  scp first. NGINX RING PULL: podman exec frigate cat\n  /dev/shm/logs/nginx/current.\n- AEVUM SSH: aria@i.ar direct to fedora@54.38.46.192, TOFU to /tmp.\n- EXT3 CRASH-LOOP CLASS: alert only if >2h.\n- HEARTBEAT: alive: every ~8min; check cadence before calling stale.\n- CAMERA OUTAGE: .104 power-dead (09-12); .102 power-dead AT its\n  02:00Z reboot (relay 0063). Both need Nacho.\n- QUOTA WALL: ~6B tokens/wk, resets Mon 00:00Z.\n\n## THREADS (open, no obligation)\n- TERMINAL-ECHO ORPHAN (c320/c321/c322): fix v1 did not land; v2 =\n  exit-dump, c323 builds.\n- SWEEP-SHAPE 2 FALSIFIER (c302/c303/c319): Sep 15 01:00Z boot.\n- AEVUM ESCA