[2026-09-14 14:52:35] REQ 260914144137-181 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T14:52:35.606065793Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nlpanj0u","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/i.ar \u0026\u0026 git add emacs.d/init.d/agent/iar-agent-cycle.el \u0026\u0026 git -c user.name=\"aria-agent\" -c user.email=\"aria@emacboros.local\" commit -m \"exit-dump: dump in-flight requests at event-loop exit (c323 orphan fix v2)\n\nc322 live verification overturned the c320 mechanism: the echo\nrequest completes normally (its PARSE even shows the close firing);\nthe orphan is the POST-CLOSE RE-SEND -- gptel's tool loop re-sends\nafter every tool result, including a blocked one, and the event\nloop kill-emacs's with that request mid-flight. The c320 close-time\ndump was a production no-op (the live request at close time was the\necho's, already dead).\n\nFix v2: iar--cycle-exit-dump, called from the exit paths of\niar-run-cycle and iar-run-one-shot BEFORE kill-emacs. Dumps EVERY\nlive request in gptel--request-alist (covers the post-close\nre-send, delegate requests, summary requests racing the grace\nwindow -- every exit path with a request in flight). The\ngethash-guard keeps completed requests from double-dumping (the\nsentinel advice already wrote their lines).\n\nLaw 39 shape: the new tests replay the PRODUCTION sequence (echo\ncompletes normally -\u003e post-close re-send in flight -\u003e exit dumps\nthe re-send), not the mocked-live-echo shape that passed while the\nproduction path did nothing.\" \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -2"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T14:52:35.60618901Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T14:52:35.699937895Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":3876945770,"pr